WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.190
Singapore, near the equator, gets
about 2,100 millimetres of rain a year.

2
00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:08.450
Tropical forest thrives.

3
00:00:08.500 --> 00:00:13.190
Alice Springs, in central Australia,
gets about 280 millimetres.

4
00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:15.390
Around it: hot desert.

5
00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:18.050
Either side of the
forest belt lies savanna:

6
00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:20.190
grass with scattered trees.

7
00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:25.110
All three lie in the hot tropics, in
rough bands parallel to the equator.

8
00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:28.590
So what decides which one grows where?

9
00:00:28.640 --> 00:00:29.650
Distance from the sea?

10
00:00:29.700 --> 00:00:31.150
The rock underneath?

11
00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:31.950
Height?

12
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:35.330
In this mission, you'll compare
climate graphs for three places,

13
00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:38.050
on one shared rainfall scale.

14
00:00:38.100 --> 00:00:40.870
Then you'll see how life
copes in each biome,

15
00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:44.710
from layered forest to desert
flowers after rare rain.

16
00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:47.770
Your mission: explain what
decides where rainforest,

17
00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:49.870
savanna and desert grow.
